{"query":"What is the exact wording in the ad regarding preexisting conditions and selling plans to any patient?","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.healthcare.gov","snippet":"All Marketplace plans must cover treatment for pre-existing medical conditions . No insurance plan can reject you, charge you more, or refuse to pay for ... Read more","title":"Marketplace health plans cover pre-existing conditions","url":"https://www.healthcare.gov/coverage/pre-existing-conditions/"},{"position":2,"site_name":"www.cigna.com","snippet":"A pre-existing condition is a medical condition that you have before starting a new health care plan . Find examples and learn more.","title":"What is a Pre-Existing Condition?","url":"https://www.cigna.com/knowledge-center/what-is-a-pre-existing-condition"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.facingourrisk.org","snippet":"The ACA bars use of pre-existing conditions . The Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (ACA) prohibits the use of pre-existing conditions —such as heart ... Read more","title":"Affordable Care Act (ACA) Pre-existing Conditions","url":"https://www.facingourrisk.org/privacy-policy-legal/laws-protections/ACA/pre-existing-conditions"},{"date":"Aug 18, 2025","position":4,"site_name":"www.uhc.com","snippet":"Aug 18, 2025 — Put simply, a pre-existing condition is a health issue you had before your current health plan started — examples could be asthma, diabetes or ... Read more","title":"Pre-existing conditions","url":"https://www.uhc.com/news-articles/benefits-and-coverage/understanding-pre-existing-conditions-and-health-coverage"},{"position":5,"site_name":"www.nationalaffairs.com","snippet":"Insurers are prohibited only from denying coverage for a pre-existing condition altogether; it is quite permissible, however, for insurance providers to charge ... Read more","title":"How to Cover Pre-existing Conditions","url":"https://www.nationalaffairs.com/publications/detail/how-to-cover-pre-existing-conditions"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.familiesusa.org","snippet":"Republicans' Empty Promises to Patients with Pre-Existing Conditions · Insurers are not allowed to deny coverage to people with pre-existing conditions . Read more","title":"Republicans' Empty Promises to Patients with Pre-Existing ...","url":"https://www.familiesusa.org/resources/republicans-empty-promises-to-patients-with-pre-existing-conditions/"},{"date":"Mar 17, 2022","position":7,"site_name":"www.hhs.gov","snippet":"Mar 17, 2022 — Under current law, health insurance companies can't refuse to cover you or charge you more just because you have a “ pre-existing condition ” ...","title":"Pre-Existing Conditions","url":"https://www.hhs.gov/healthcare/about-the-aca/pre-existing-conditions/index.html"},{"position":8,"site_name":"www.gaucherdisease.org","snippet":"Living with a rare disease, such as Gaucher disease, may make selecting health insurance a challenge. Read our tips for finding the best plan for you.","title":"7 Tips for Selecting Health Insurance with a Pre-Existing ...","url":"https://www.gaucherdisease.org/blog/selecting-health-insurance-when-you-have-a-rare-disease/"},{"position":9,"site_name":"www.healthinsurance.org","snippet":"What is a pre-existing condition ? An illness or injury experienced before enrollment in a health insurance plan may be considered a pre-existing condition . Read more","title":"What is a pre-existing condition?","url":"https://www.healthinsurance.org/glossary/pre-existing-condition/"}],"total_results":9,"page":0}